tests: free the contexts of the recurrent rollback test on each return path
Fold-into: fuzz-core/0003-tests-state-the-rollback-depth-rule-in-the-recurrent-state-test.patch

The defects. The ctest entries of test-recurrent-state-rollback show each one in an ASan build.

- A failed check of test_rollback leaks its contexts.

  test_rollback frees ctx_src, ctx_dst and ctx_dirty only at its end. Each failed check returns
  before that, thus LeakSanitizer reports the contexts on top of the failure, and the report hides
  the failure. test_multi_seq_split_replay leaks the context that it created when the other one
  fails to initialize.

  The change: llama_context_ptr owners free the three contexts of test_rollback on each return
  path. The owners release them before the multi-sequence part, as the explicit frees did. The
  init failure of the multi-sequence part calls its cleanup.

  The test: ctest test-recurrent-state-rollback and its model entries in an ASan build.

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 with the patches of patches/series above this one.

